From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jinbo Zhang <jinboz1@uci.edu>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 17:22:03 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 2/7] ConnectedComponents: on_true_graph_edges selects edges
 with edge_y

The dataset renames y -> edge_y, so graph.y is None when _build_event
runs and graph.edge_index[:, None] keeps every edge. The "perfect scores"
option therefore produced one giant component (14,341 hits on a TrackML
event) instead of the true-edge components.

gd-displaced patch 0002 (plan item b).
---
 acorn/stages/track_building/models/connected_components.py | 5 ++++-
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/acorn/stages/track_building/models/connected_components.py b/acorn/stages/track_building/models/connected_components.py
index 06c2b03a..e914dffe 100644
--- a/acorn/stages/track_building/models/connected_components.py
+++ b/acorn/stages/track_building/models/connected_components.py
@@ -78,7 +78,10 @@ class ConnectedComponents(TrackBuildingStage):
         if on_truth_particle_edges:
             edges = graph.track_edges
         elif on_true_graph_edges:
-            edges = graph.edge_index[:, graph.y]
+            # GraphDataset renames y -> edge_y, so graph.y is None here and
+            # edge_index[:, None] silently kept every edge (one giant component).
+            truth = graph.edge_y if "edge_y" in graph else graph.y
+            edges = graph.edge_index[:, truth.bool()]
         else:
             edge_mask = graph.edge_scores > score_cut
             edges = graph.edge_index[:, edge_mask]
